3,Amahuaca - Summary - eHRAF World Cultures,https://ehrafworldcultures.yale.edu/cultures/se06/summary,"The language of the Amahuaca is Panoan. It is most similar to that of the neighboring Yaminahua, has slight regional variations, and is believed to have separated from Conibo about a thousand years ago.",Amahuaca,Panoan
4,"Amahuaca language, alphabet and pronunciation - OmniglotAmahuaca - Summary - eHRAF World Cultures1. Description headwater streams of the Javari, Juruá, Purus ...Peruvian amazon music: Amahuaca / Música de la amazonía ...Universal Dependencies for Amahuaca - ACL Anthology",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/amahuaca.htm,"Amahuaca is a tonal language with two tones: high and low. The high tone can be marked with an acute accent (á), and the low tone is not marked. Source: http://www.native-languages.org/amahuaca_guide.htm Download an Amahuaca alphabet chart(Excel) See full list on omniglot.com Tzovan jato jumahaito hinaayamanonmun vacunoxcanquihnucanpu. Tzovan jato zinaayamanonmun vacunoxcanquihnucanpu. Jonitzan derechocavizyahtoxrivimun vacunoxcanquihqui. Quiyoovinin shinanquin hiromaquin jaucuzahavorahquiqui shinantimunhcanquihqui. Vacurazixquicavizhi quiyoovinixjatimunhcanquihnucanpu. See full list on omniglot.com Information about the Amahuaca language http://www.native-languages.org/amahuaca.htm http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amahuaca_language http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idioma_amahuaca See full list on omniglot.com Amahuaca, Kashibo, Kashinawa, Matsés, Shipibo, Yaminawa Languages written with the Latin alphabet Page last modified: 17.11.22 [top] You can support this site by Buying Me A Coffee, and if you like what you see on this page, you can use the buttons below to share it with people you know. If you like this site and find it useful, you can support it ... See full list on omniglot.com The language of the Amahuaca is Panoan. It is most similar to that of the neighboring Yaminahua, has slight regional variations, and is believed to have separated from Conibo about a thousand years ago. 2.9 Food taboos: 2.10 Canoes/watercraft? Canoes cannot make it through the waters so they use rafts made of balsa logs. In certain areas where the Amahuaca are found they do use canoes, Purus, Sepahua, and Ucayali. Apr 26, 2009 · The Amahuaca native group belongs to the Panoan language family of peruvian amazon. This group is widely scattered throughout the southeastern part of the Amazon Basin in the states of Ucayali and Madre de Dios. This paper presents the creation of a Universal Dependency (UD) treebank for Amahuaca (Peru), marking the first UD treebank within the Headwaters subbranch of the Panoan family, spoken mostly in Peru and Brazil. Is Amahuaca a Panoan language? Amahuaca is a Panoan language spoken by about 250 people in Peru and Brazil. It is also known as Amawaka, Amaguaco, Ameuhaque, Ipitineri and Sayaco, and is closely related to Kashinawa and Shipibo. The Amahuaca dialects include Inuvaken and Viwivaken. The name Amahuaca refer to the Capivara River in Brazil, along which the Amahuaca people live. Who are the Amahuaca shamans? The Amahuaca are one group of Indigenous Amazonians in which shamans are known to use ayahuasca in ritual ceremonies, typically for the purpose of entering the realm of spirits and deceased relatives or ancestors. The use of this drug is not recreational, but rather spiritual. Where did the Amahuaca come from? They originally had no name for themselves as a people other than hondi kuí (real people) or yora (human beings). The Amahuaca are sparsely settled on the Inuya and Sepahua rivers, and on headwater streams of the Javari, Juruá, Purus and Piedras rivers, in a deeply dissected limestone plateau on the border of Peru and Brazil. Where do Amahuaca live? The Amahuaca are sparsely settled on the Inuya and Sepahua rivers, and on headwater streams of the Javari, Juruá, Purus and Piedras rivers, in a deeply dissected limestone plateau on the border of Peru and Brazil. Annual rainfall of 177 to 203 centimeters between October and April supports unbroken tropical forest with abundant game.",Amahuaca,Panoan
